WEBVTT

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:47.047
So, what happened to Gedosh? Is he okay?

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.298
Dunno.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:51.176
You don't know? You really don't know?!

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:56.556
This deal is between the boss and us.
We do as he says and we get paid.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:01:00.769
And when it's done,
we get a bonus. That's how it works.

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:03.938
Are you guys mercenaries or something?

00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:07.025
Something close to that, I guess.

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:08.234
They're coming.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.070
I can see that, too.

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:14.115
How long till we get to the hotel?

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:15.742
Ten minutes.

00:01:17.952 --> 00:01:20.955
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself </i>

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:24.542
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:34.511
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:37.889
<i>Roaming around the city having lost my map</i>

00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:41.226
<i>Even a dying world</i>

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:48.024
<i>Let me hear a life deep</i>
<i>within that won't stop running</i>

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:50.985
<i>I seared the undying light into my eyes</i>

00:01:50.985 --> 00:01:54.531
<i>Refusing to shut them</i>
<i>even when they dried</i>

00:01:54.531 --> 00:02:01.204
<i>I don't believe anything I</i>
<i>can obtain without getting hurt</i>

00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:07.419
<i>A single emotion</i>
<i>directed toward someone</i>

00:02:07.419 --> 00:02:14.718
<i>Splits the steel darkness</i>
<i>like the light of morning</i>

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:19.389
<i>One day brave your</i>
<i>truth and brave yourself</i>

00:02:19.389 --> 00:02:22.934
<i>So you will drastically change</i>

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:28.690
<i>Compounded strength and prayers</i>

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.444
<i>Intersecting futures</i>
<i>and wishes held close</i>

00:02:32.444 --> 00:02:36.031
<i>I will give these to no one</i>

00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:37.532
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:42.746
<i>It links our hearts</i>

00:02:49.878 --> 00:02:52.672
Felli... Didn't come, did she?

00:02:53.923 --> 00:02:58.511
Maybe she caught a cold or something.

00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:07.520
That's all for today's training.

00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:09.898
Nina?

00:03:10.357 --> 00:03:11.941
See ya!

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:16.029
All right! You free now, new guy?

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:18.615
I have to work this evening, but...

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:21.368
You're free, right? That's right, right?!

00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:23.536
We were lucky enough to have met...

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:26.373
We should spend time to <i>deepen </i>that friendship.

00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:29.584
Uh, but I have my job...

00:03:29.793 --> 00:03:33.296
"Disarmament! Put on That Maid's Outfit!"

00:03:38.259 --> 00:03:38.760
Wel...

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.219
Come...

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:39.594
Cust...

00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:40.011
To...

00:03:40.011 --> 00:03:41.846
Mer!

00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:44.933
And a heart-pounding rice omelette
for you as well, right? Understood!

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:47.602
May I take your order please?

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:50.230
Here you are.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:54.901
Nice, huh? All these cute girls
should be on the World Heritage List.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.861
So, why did you bring me here?

00:03:56.861 --> 00:03:58.446
Welcome.

00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:07.789
Your order?

00:04:07.872 --> 00:04:11.501
Senior Felli, what are you doing?

00:04:14.963 --> 00:04:16.089
My stomach!

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.966
My stomach hurts!

00:04:19.134 --> 00:04:20.969
<i>Your</i>. <i>Order?</i>

00:04:27.142 --> 00:04:28.977
I was careless!

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:37.193
My first mistake was being
discovered while looking for a job.

00:04:37.193 --> 00:04:42.032
You're looking for job?
I'll show ya a great place.

00:04:42.032 --> 00:04:45.702
Thinking I could trust that man...

00:04:47.203 --> 00:04:49.039
Just you wait!

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.384
About the place we spoke of...

00:05:01.384 --> 00:05:04.763
Just to be sure, I'll go there
tonight for final confirmation.

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.473
Please do, Vanzeh.

00:05:06.473 --> 00:05:09.768
I could see nothing amiss
in the previous inspection,

00:05:09.768 --> 00:05:13.229
so I think there's no cause for concern.

00:05:18.193 --> 00:05:20.445
Wait juuuust a minute...

00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:23.656
Ah, there she is! Here.

00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:35.168
Your order?

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.461
Two coffees.

00:05:36.461 --> 00:05:39.089
And maybe your love-

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.553
I will return shortly.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:49.766
'Scuse me!

00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:53.853
N-No, it's nothing.

00:05:58.525 --> 00:06:01.361
Felli-<i>chan</i>, no no <i>no</i>.

00:06:01.778 --> 00:06:07.033
We need pearly whites!
Show the customer your very best smile!

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.703
You work hard and you're a fast learner,

00:06:09.703 --> 00:06:12.706
but your face is a bit stiff...

00:06:14.624 --> 00:06:18.211
Why don't you try practicing a little?

00:06:18.712 --> 00:06:20.380
Welcome.

00:06:25.093 --> 00:06:26.761
Welcome.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.596
Welcome.

00:06:28.596 --> 00:06:32.600
--Dude... Have you ever seen Felli-<i>chan </i>smile?
--Welcome.

00:06:36.021 --> 00:06:41.026
They say nen'i operators
are bad at expressing emotion.

00:06:41.443 --> 00:06:46.781
They get a lot of information
going into their heads, right?

00:06:46.781 --> 00:06:51.036
If they reacted to every single
thing, their emotions couldn't handle it.

00:06:51.036 --> 00:06:55.665
Before they know it, they've
blocked off their emotional responses.

00:06:55.665 --> 00:06:59.085
I... I've heard that before.

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:03.048
Being surprised, angry, even laughing...

00:07:03.048 --> 00:07:08.970
It's all processed in the head, making
them expressionless. Hence the smile!

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:13.600
Felli-<i>chan</i>'s popular! If I can get
an ultra-rare picture of her smiling,

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.186
I can sell it for a good price!

00:07:16.978 --> 00:07:19.856
Well, shall we give it a try?

00:07:19.856 --> 00:07:22.192
W-Welcome.

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:28.365
I suppose there's no point in forcing it, hm?

00:07:28.365 --> 00:07:32.827
Well, fine. Let's go the
"attractive but aloof" route.

00:07:36.039 --> 00:07:38.667
And that means...

00:07:44.172 --> 00:07:46.174
Yahoo!

00:07:55.433 --> 00:07:57.060
Welcome.

00:07:57.644 --> 00:08:00.063
Iced coffee, please.

00:08:00.647 --> 00:08:02.023
Your order?

00:08:02.023 --> 00:08:03.650
Uh, coffee...

00:08:08.071 --> 00:08:10.407
My prototype new design...

00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:15.036
As I thought, paired with that
aloof expression, it's to <i>die </i>for!

00:08:26.715 --> 00:08:28.341
Excuse me.

00:08:31.261 --> 00:08:35.515
Miss Waitress. Tea and cake, please. Hurry.

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:50.071
What are you doing?

00:08:50.071 --> 00:08:55.368
Uh, as student council president,
I am observing the public morality.

00:08:56.703 --> 00:09:01.958
Tea and cake, wasn't it? I will return shortly.

00:09:04.836 --> 00:09:07.839
Felli-<i>chan</i>... It hurts...

00:09:08.882 --> 00:09:10.216
I'm going to go ho--

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:13.219
Huh? What's going on with Felli-<i>chan</i>?

00:09:14.262 --> 00:09:16.264
What are you doing?

00:09:26.274 --> 00:09:27.901
Fine, here.

00:09:29.694 --> 00:09:30.737
Ow!

00:09:30.737 --> 00:09:32.280
Ow ow ow!

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.698
Uh, I--

00:09:33.698 --> 00:09:39.454
I know. From now on,
do not associate with those of little character.

00:09:39.454 --> 00:09:41.706
That was pretty rough, Felli-<i>chan</i>!

00:09:44.542 --> 00:09:48.380
Why do I end up using this...?

00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:53.259
Excuse me.

00:10:06.147 --> 00:10:07.732
Senior Felli...

00:10:10.735 --> 00:10:12.362
Fon-Fon.

00:10:13.196 --> 00:10:15.407
Have you forgotten?

00:10:15.407 --> 00:10:19.577
Oh. Uh... Felli...

00:10:19.577 --> 00:10:20.829
What is it?

00:10:20.829 --> 00:10:23.581
Why did you suddenly want to start working?

00:10:23.581 --> 00:10:29.212
It was not sudden. I'd been
considering it for quite some time.

00:10:31.214 --> 00:10:34.759
Since I was a child,
my parents and those around me

00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:38.263
have thought that being
a nen'i operator is my only path.

00:10:39.097 --> 00:10:41.641
But I don't think so.

00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:45.729
I know that people can decide their own futures,

00:10:45.729 --> 00:10:50.567
so I came to Zuellni to search for my own path.

00:10:50.984 --> 00:10:52.652
However...

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:56.614
You said it yourself, didn't you Fon-Fon?

00:10:57.741 --> 00:11:03.163
I don't think I should stay this way either.

00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:18.595
Let's get the lunch special!

00:11:18.595 --> 00:11:19.721
Yeah.

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:20.930
It's good isn't it?

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:21.681
Yeah.

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:22.849
Let's order a dessert, too.

00:11:22.849 --> 00:11:24.517
Yeah!

00:11:24.517 --> 00:11:26.686
Have you taken a liking to it?

00:11:27.854 --> 00:11:32.942
Fresh baked! Delicious,
<i>delicious </i>fresh-baked bread!

00:11:35.236 --> 00:11:37.530
I can't do something like that!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:40.533
Yeah, I don't think we
could do a job like that...

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:46.873
It'll be all right! Don't go
overthinking this! C'mon, please!

00:11:46.873 --> 00:11:48.541
But, but...

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.545
Senior Felli.

00:11:52.545 --> 00:11:54.547
I will do it.

00:11:56.007 --> 00:11:59.719
That job. I will do it, too.

00:12:07.435 --> 00:12:10.897
This is the old research
building of the Alchemy Department.

00:12:10.897 --> 00:12:15.110
They say that thirty years ago, there
was a big accident during an experiment!

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:18.071
People were injured or even killed,
and this was locked down!

00:12:18.071 --> 00:12:21.449
But for some reason the
building was never torn down,

00:12:21.449 --> 00:12:25.662
and rumor says the spirits
of the victims roam these halls!

00:12:26.579 --> 00:12:32.502
And so! On-the-scene reporting
with some of the general public!

00:12:32.502 --> 00:12:36.423
In other words, uh,
a story for the Weekly Look'N.

00:12:39.134 --> 00:12:40.510
I wonder if she's angry.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:43.596
I knew it would be rude
to have her do a job like this...

00:12:43.596 --> 00:12:46.766
Huh?! But she was the one
who said she wanted to come!

00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:48.977
I understand our purpose here.

00:12:50.061 --> 00:12:52.188
Nice! It looks like she's not mad.

00:12:52.188 --> 00:12:55.316
But isn't this building off limits?

00:12:55.734 --> 00:13:00.697
Don't be such a stick in the mud!
This comes with being an ace reporter!

00:13:00.697 --> 00:13:05.535
I want to be a policeman,
so I don't think I should be involved.

00:13:08.204 --> 00:13:14.711
If you want to be a policeman,
you have to protect the public, right?

00:13:17.339 --> 00:13:19.090
May, what did you bring?

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.092
Um, a boxed lunch.

00:13:21.092 --> 00:13:24.179
A boxed lunch? To a haunted spot?!

00:13:24.179 --> 00:13:28.016
I thought we might get hungry,
so I brought sandwiches...

00:13:28.016 --> 00:13:30.518
Great, there goes the mood!

00:13:30.518 --> 00:13:33.646
Let's eat later. What do you say, Senior Felli?

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:35.565
Her food is delicious.

00:13:35.565 --> 00:13:38.818
She researches by eating from
restaurants with great food, right?

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:39.569
Don't get fat!

00:13:39.569 --> 00:13:41.863
Cut it out, Mii-<i>chan</i>!

00:13:41.863 --> 00:13:42.864
How scary!

00:13:42.864 --> 00:13:45.492
What a great locale... Photograph a ghost!

00:13:46.451 --> 00:13:48.787
Mii! Hurry up and finish!

00:13:48.787 --> 00:13:52.624
The editor told me to take a bunch to send in!

00:13:55.418 --> 00:13:59.297
Sorry. Being a reporter has been Mii's dream.

00:13:59.297 --> 00:14:01.466
She's so happy that she's beside herself.

00:14:02.008 --> 00:14:03.426
Dream...

00:14:03.426 --> 00:14:08.848
The other day, I put in a work
request to the municipal police.

00:14:08.848 --> 00:14:11.184
So you can work on the police force?

00:14:11.184 --> 00:14:15.188
I don't know yet, but
I can't lose out to Mii or you!

00:14:15.188 --> 00:14:17.857
You'll do fine, Nakki.

00:14:17.857 --> 00:14:19.401
I hope so.

00:14:19.401 --> 00:14:21.528
But it's pretty difficult.

00:14:24.364 --> 00:14:26.700
I wonder if I've gotten some good photos...

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.035
Oh! Maybe I should get over there, too!

00:14:29.035 --> 00:14:30.704
U-Um...

00:14:32.205 --> 00:14:33.790
Sandwich?

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.625
If you like...

00:14:42.799 --> 00:14:44.217
Mii-<i>chan</i>?

00:14:44.217 --> 00:14:45.844
Mii!

00:14:52.934 --> 00:14:54.853
What is this?

00:14:54.853 --> 00:14:57.772
Mii-<i>chan</i>? Mii-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:07.532 --> 00:15:09.159
Look out!

00:15:38.063 --> 00:15:39.689
Vanzeh...

00:15:42.192 --> 00:15:44.194
This way, Felli!

00:15:50.033 --> 00:15:52.535
What are you doing somewhere like this?

00:15:52.535 --> 00:15:55.497
What are <i>you</i>? And what was that?

00:15:55.497 --> 00:15:59.542
Thirty years ago, there was a plan
to create an artificial life form

00:15:59.542 --> 00:16:03.546
to combat the contaminoids.

00:16:03.546 --> 00:16:06.383
They were the protectoids.
The Guardian Project.

00:16:06.383 --> 00:16:08.301
The Guardian Project?

00:16:08.301 --> 00:16:11.805
But after multiple failures,
the project was suspended.

00:16:11.805 --> 00:16:14.516
Apparently, this research
building was to be decommissioned.

00:16:14.516 --> 00:16:17.060
So that creature was a Guardian?

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:21.356
I don't know. Kalian decided
this building was to be torn down

00:16:21.356 --> 00:16:25.819
and has been making sure
nothing dangerous was left behind.

00:16:25.819 --> 00:16:30.657
Those creatures weren't here
the last time I came. What's going on?

00:16:30.657 --> 00:16:32.701
You came here alone?

00:16:32.701 --> 00:16:36.246
With a few others. They were taken.

00:16:36.246 --> 00:16:41.126
But why? You should have
detected those monsters approaching!

00:16:41.126 --> 00:16:44.295
I was not using nen'i.

00:16:44.295 --> 00:16:47.632
I don't know what's going on here,
but this is a critical situation.

00:16:47.632 --> 00:16:54.472
Use your nen'i terminal to track
who was captured. Request backup!

00:16:56.349 --> 00:17:00.020
Hurry! Your comrades' lives depend on it!

00:17:02.856 --> 00:17:04.524
Restoration.

00:17:26.338 --> 00:17:27.714
I found them! They're in the basement.

00:17:27.714 --> 00:17:32.177
I'm picking up bioactivity.
They seem to have been put to sleep.

00:17:40.727 --> 00:17:42.354
Get back!

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:07.796
Senior Felli?

00:18:08.713 --> 00:18:10.382
The Guardian Project.

00:18:10.382 --> 00:18:12.175
What's the situation?

00:18:12.175 --> 00:18:14.260
It seems to be a tough battle.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:18.682
We're coming now! And listen,
don't do anything foolish!

00:18:36.032 --> 00:18:38.368
Why do I...

00:18:38.368 --> 00:18:40.370
Why? Why?

00:18:47.043 --> 00:18:48.670
Felli!

00:19:09.482 --> 00:19:11.109
Now.

00:19:48.688 --> 00:19:51.358
Some old chemicals leaked from their bottles...

00:19:51.358 --> 00:19:54.069
Did I faint?

00:19:54.069 --> 00:19:57.906
This is because you were
trespassing in a restricted area.

00:19:57.906 --> 00:20:01.368
So I can write an article
about our experience...

00:20:01.368 --> 00:20:03.620
I can't, can I?

00:20:07.957 --> 00:20:09.793
Senior Felli!

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:16.800
I'm glad you're all right!

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.260
Did I not inform you of such?

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.846
Yes, you did. But I'm really glad.

00:20:21.846 --> 00:20:23.264
Felli!

00:20:23.431 --> 00:20:27.018
Are you all right? I told you not
to do anything foolish, didn't I?!

00:20:27.018 --> 00:20:31.272
It looks like you're not injured.
I'm glad. I'm so glad!

00:20:31.272 --> 00:20:35.276
I'm sorry I didn't make it in time.
I was worried about you!

00:20:36.361 --> 00:20:39.906
Felli has been a genius since she was a child.

00:20:39.906 --> 00:20:43.284
She doesn't know the meaning of hardship.

00:20:43.284 --> 00:20:47.706
She says she searches for her
own path, but she hasn't done anything.

00:20:47.706 --> 00:20:51.126
She says she resents me, yet we live together.

00:20:51.126 --> 00:20:52.711
She's a child.

00:20:52.711 --> 00:20:55.630
And yet, she took action.

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:56.798
Why?

00:20:56.798 --> 00:21:02.053
What a waste... All it does is hurt her.

00:21:02.053 --> 00:21:05.765
Is that why you put your sister
in the Military Arts Department?

00:21:05.765 --> 00:21:07.350
To watch over her?

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:09.853
Of course, that was not the only reason.

00:21:09.853 --> 00:21:11.855
You're overprotective.

00:21:13.898 --> 00:21:18.737
In any case, we can only
assume that was a sealed Guardian.

00:21:18.737 --> 00:21:21.364
Why would it rejuvenate <i>now</i>?

00:21:22.907 --> 00:21:24.743
Troublesome, isn't it?

00:21:32.083 --> 00:21:33.918
It's delicious.

00:21:35.587 --> 00:21:40.050
Those girls... I saw them so brightly.

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:42.052
I dragged you into this, didn't I?

00:21:42.052 --> 00:21:44.721
Not at all. By the way, ma'am...

00:21:44.721 --> 00:21:48.975
Uh, Felli, did you find your path?

00:21:48.975 --> 00:21:54.397
You would ask that after I'd
been placed in such a situation?

00:21:55.023 --> 00:21:58.193
You're right. Sorry.

00:22:07.952 --> 00:22:09.245
You saw that, didn't you?

00:22:09.245 --> 00:22:12.499
Uh, well...

00:22:12.499 --> 00:22:17.962
<i>Ow ow ow! Ow! Ow...</i>

00:22:35.230 --> 00:22:38.024
<i>Beyond memory</i>

00:22:38.024 --> 00:22:46.366
<i>A map of the ideal future</i>
<i>you'd been searching for</i>

00:22:46.366 --> 00:22:57.377
<i>Scared of something, not</i>
<i>understanding, trembling alone</i>

00:22:57.377 --> 00:23:08.763
<i>Unable to see you, I'm</i>
<i>always wearing a fake smile</i>

